BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Comprehensive Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 536.60 24.00 Td (1) Tj ET
BT /F2 18 Tf 54.00 762.00 Td (Comprehensive Interview Questions And Answers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 727.00 Td (Project: Multi-Rail Power Management Board) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 710.00 Td (Use case: hardware, embedded systems, power electronics, LTspice, KiCad, bring-up, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 696.00 Td (debugging interviews) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 665.00 Td (How To Use This Document) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 636.00 Td (Start with the easy questions until the project story feels natural. Then move to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 622.00 Td (intermediate and advanced sections. In an interview, do not recite everything. Give a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 608.00 Td (direct answer first, then expand only if the interviewer asks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 577.00 Td (Easy Level: Project Basics) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 548.00 Td (1. What is this project about?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 524.00 Td (It is a multi-rail power management board. It takes a 5 V input and generates three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 510.00 Td (sequenced rails: 1.2 V, 1.8 V, and 3.3 V for an SoC plus sensor cluster.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 487.00 Td (2. Why did you build it?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 463.00 Td (I built it to demonstrate power-rail planning, sequencing, LTspice simulation, KiCad) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 449.00 Td (schematic capture, BOM creation, and hardware bring-up thinking.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 426.00 Td (3. What are the output voltages?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 402.00 Td (The outputs are 1.2 V, 1.8 V, and 3.3 V.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 379.00 Td (4. What does each rail power?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 355.00 Td (The 1.2 V rail represents SoC core logic, the 1.8 V rail represents I/O logic, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 341.00 Td (3.3 V rail represents sensors or camera peripherals.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 318.00 Td (5. What is the input voltage?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 294.00 Td (The input is a nominal 5 V supply, similar to USB or a bench supply.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 271.00 Td (6. What is power sequencing?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 247.00 Td (Power sequencing is turning power rails on and off in a controlled order.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 224.00 Td (7. What is the startup order?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 200.00 Td (The 1.2 V core rail starts first, the 1.8 V I/O rail starts second, and the 3.3 V sensor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 186.00 Td (rail starts third.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 163.00 Td (8. Why does the core rail start first?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 139.00 Td (The core logic should be alive before I/O and peripherals are powered. This reduces the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 125.00 Td (risk of back-powering, undefined logic states, and latch-up.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 102.00 Td (9. What tools did you use?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 78.00 Td (I used LTspice for simulation and KiCad for schematic capture and ERC checking.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
