stream
BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Comprehensive Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 536.60 24.00 Td (4) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 772.00 Td (35. What does the 22 uF output capacitor do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 748.00 Td (It provides local charge, reduces ripple, and helps reduce voltage droop during) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 734.00 Td (transient events.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 711.00 Td (36. Why use X7R ceramic capacitors?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 687.00 Td (X7R capacitors have better temperature stability than lower-grade dielectrics and are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 673.00 Td (common for decoupling.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 650.00 Td (37. What is ESR?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 626.00 Td (ESR is equivalent series resistance. It is the effective resistance inside a capacitor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 612.00 Td (and affects ripple and transient voltage drop.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 589.00 Td (38. What is ESL?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 565.00 Td (ESL is equivalent series inductance. It limits how well a capacitor responds at very) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 551.00 Td (high frequencies.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 528.00 Td (39. Why place capacitors near regulator pins?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 504.00 Td (Short placement reduces parasitic inductance and resistance, improving transient) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 490.00 Td (response and reducing noise.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 467.00 Td (40. Why include reverse-polarity protection?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 443.00 Td (It protects the board if the input supply is connected backwards.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 420.00 Td (41. What is the downside of a Schottky diode for input protection?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 396.00 Td (It has a forward voltage drop and dissipates heat.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 373.00 Td (42. What is a better production reverse-protection method?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 349.00 Td (A P-MOSFET ideal-diode style circuit or ideal diode controller gives lower voltage drop) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 335.00 Td (and better efficiency.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 312.00 Td (43. Why include a P-MOSFET load switch?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 288.00 Td (It allows the sensor rail to be disconnected, sequenced, or power-gated.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 265.00 Td (44. What does an enable pin do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 241.00 Td (An enable pin turns a regulator on or off.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 218.00 Td (45. How can an RC delay create sequencing?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 194.00 Td (A resistor charges a capacitor. The regulator enable pin turns on when the capacitor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 180.00 Td (voltage crosses its threshold.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 157.00 Td (46. What is the approximate RC delay formula?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 133.00 Td (For a charging capacitor, `t = -RC ln\(1 - Vth/Vin\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 110.00 Td (47. Why are RC delays not exact?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 86.00 Td (They vary with resistor tolerance, capacitor tolerance, leakage, temperature, and enable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 72.00 Td (threshold variation.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 26 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 595 842] /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R /F2 2 0 R /F3 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 10 0 R >>
