12 0 obj
<< /Length 3009 >>
stream
BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Comprehensive Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 536.60 24.00 Td (5) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 772.00 Td (48. What is better than RC sequencing for production?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 748.00 Td (A power sequencer IC, supervisor, PMIC, or microcontroller-controlled enable sequence is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 734.00 Td (more precise.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 711.00 Td (49. Why include test points on enable nets?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 687.00 Td (Enable test points let me verify that the sequence is actually happening at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 673.00 Td (regulator control pins.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 650.00 Td (50. Why include test points on every rail?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 626.00 Td (They make bring-up and debugging easier because every important voltage can be probed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 612.00 Td (directly.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 581.00 Td (Intermediate Level: LTspice And Simulation) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 552.00 Td (51. Why use behavioral sources in LTspice?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 528.00 Td (Behavioral sources make the architecture easy to simulate without getting blocked by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 514.00 Td (fragile vendor model setup.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 491.00 Td (52. Does the behavioral simulation model real switching ripple?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 467.00 Td (No. It models startup timing and load behavior, but not actual buck switching ripple or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 453.00 Td (compensation loop details.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 430.00 Td (53. Why is that acceptable for this stage?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (At the architecture stage, the main goal is to verify sequencing and load response) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 392.00 Td (conceptually. Detailed regulator simulation can come later.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 369.00 Td (54. What does `.tran 20m startup` do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 345.00 Td (It runs a transient simulation for 20 ms and starts from initial startup conditions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 322.00 Td (55. What signals should be plotted?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 298.00 Td (Plot the three rail voltages and the three enable signals: `V\(RAIL_A_1V2\)`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 284.00 Td (`V\(RAIL_B_1V8\)`, `V\(RAIL_C_3V3\)`, `V\(EN_A\)`, `V\(EN_B\)`, and `V\(EN_C\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 261.00 Td (56. What do the `.meas` commands do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 237.00 Td (They automatically measure rail startup times and Rail C voltage behavior) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 223.00 Td (before/during/after the load step.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 200.00 Td (57. Why measure 90% rail time?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 176.00 Td (90% of nominal is a common practical threshold for determining when a rail is mostly up.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 153.00 Td (58. What is 90% of 1.2 V?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 129.00 Td (`0.9 * 1.2 = 1.08 V`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 106.00 Td (59. What is 90% of 1.8 V?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 82.00 Td (`0.9 * 1.8 = 1.62 V`.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
