stream
BT /F2 8 Tf 54.00 814.00 Td (Comprehensive Interview Q&A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 536.60 24.00 Td (6) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 772.00 Td (60. What is 90% of 3.3 V?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 748.00 Td (`0.9 * 3.3 = 2.97 V`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 725.00 Td (61. Why did you move long formulas into `.func` directives?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 701.00 Td (To keep the LTspice schematic visually clean. The source values stay short, while the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 687.00 Td (detailed equations live in a directive block.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 664.00 Td (62. What is the purpose of `V=RA\(time\)`?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 640.00 Td (It tells the behavioral source to output the Rail A voltage according to the `RA\(t\)`) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 626.00 Td (function.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 603.00 Td (63. Why are enable signals included as separate sources?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 579.00 Td (They make the intended sequence visible in the waveform plot.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 556.00 Td (64. How would you improve the simulation for production?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 532.00 Td (Use verified manufacturer models, include inductors and feedback components, model input) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 518.00 Td (supply ramp, include ESR/ESL, and run corner cases.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 495.00 Td (65. What corner cases would you simulate?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 471.00 Td (Minimum/maximum input voltage, light/full load, startup into load, output short) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 457.00 Td (behavior, temperature extremes, capacitor tolerance, and sequencing tolerance.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54.00 426.00 Td (Advanced Level: Regulator And Power Electronics) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 397.00 Td (66. Why might an LDO from 5 V to 1.2 V be thermally bad?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 373.00 Td (The power loss is `\(5 - 1.2\) * 0.5 = 1.9 W`, which is too high for many small packages.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 350.00 Td (67. What would you use instead for high-current 1.2 V?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 326.00 Td (I would use a buck converter, possibly followed by a low-noise LDO if the rail needs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 312.00 Td (extra filtering.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 289.00 Td (68. What is buck converter efficiency?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 265.00 Td (Efficiency is output power divided by input power. A buck converter is usually much more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 251.00 Td (efficient than an LDO for high voltage drop and high current.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 228.00 Td (69. What is the purpose of the inductor in a buck converter?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 204.00 Td (The inductor stores and releases energy each switching cycle, smoothing current and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 190.00 Td (enabling efficient voltage conversion.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 167.00 Td (70. What happens if the inductor is too small?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 143.00 Td (Ripple current increases, which can increase ripple, losses, current stress, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 129.00 Td (possibly instability.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54.00 106.00 Td (71. What happens if the inductor is too large?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54.00 82.00 Td (Transient response can become slower, size and cost increase, and the regulator may not) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
